{"term":"flourish","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1096fdad44d2d7cf85","definition":"To thrive or grow well.","example":"The barley flourished in the warm weather.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2198b7c9e5ea6e185","definition":"To prosper or fare well.","example":"The town flourished with the coming of the railway.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:128366a133d6c48a08","definition":"To be in a period of greatest influence.","example":"His writing flourished before the war.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:876cbf7e4d05728330","definition":"To develop; to make thrive; to expand.","example":"But all that I ſhall ſay in this vvhole Argument, vvill be but like Bottomes of Thred, cloſe vvound vp, vvhich vvith a good Needle (perhaps) may be flouriſhed into large VVorkes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d95321024740709c8f","definition":"To make bold, sweeping movements with.","example":"They flourished the banner as they stormed the palace.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:64f6d970183111f0ac","definition":"To make bold and sweeping, fanciful, or wanton movements, by way of ornament, parade, bravado, etc.; to play with fantastic and irregular motion.","example":"Impetuous spread the stream, and smoking flourished o'er his head.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourishment","flourishy","outflourish","overflourish","reflourish","unflourished"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0dcdaccd32add763aa","definition":"To use florid language; to indulge in rhetorical figures and lofty expressions.","example":"They dilate […] and flourish long upon little incidents.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["flourishable","flourisher","flourishly","flourish